 STEP 2. PUSH ENGAGEMENTS ONTO THE BOARDS
 Push Engagements onto the boards. The team curates (decision 185). A guest belongs on the board for its Show when the Engagement has Host board ticked (the team's choice; never tick or untick it yourself) OR Status is Booking or Booked (the one automatic rule), OR Status is Recorded or Form filled with Next date in the last 60 days and the guest was already on the board. For each such Engagement with Show un#, B2S or HBD, find its board row by the Engagement relation, else OS key; create it if missing (Guest "<name> @ <company>", Engagement, OS key, Eval as in STEP 3, Short pitch, Guest availability and Eval link as in STEP 3, LinkedIn, and the EVAL SNAPSHOT in the page body). A new row at Approval pending is a question to the host: unless Next action already asks it, add the host to Waiting on and "<Host>: your call on <guest> on your board" after any open ask (" | "). Stage: on un# from 19 Oct 2026 08:00 JST, a guest Akshay hasn't decided on (any open Status before Booking, Precall done included) stays Approval pending whatever Host approval says: Sri's Yes never stands in for his verdict. Otherwise Booked -> Scheduled with Recording date = Next date; Booking, or Precall done with Host approval Yes -> To be scheduled; Host approval Yes and any other open Status -> In touch; Host approval empty or Not asked -> Approval pending; Recorded or Form filled with Next date in the last 60 days -> Recorded. Set Stage Not now on any board row whose Engagement no longer belongs on the board by that rule, is closed, has Host approval No (on un# from 19 Oct 2026 08:00 JST only once the Engagement is closed: Sri's No alone leaves the Stage as it is), or was recorded more than 60 days ago. Don't overwrite what the host typed (<Host>'s call, notes, availability).
